; PLAN_liquid_types.md L2: the Liquid Austral refinement AST (`LiquidTypes`),
; the TRL contract-string parser (`LiquidParse`), and the `liquid` compiler
; pass (`LiquidCheck`).
;
; This is a separate library rather than more `austral_core` modules because the
; pass sits on the `Compiler_plugin` seam, which `austral_lib` owns: `austral`
; the library depends on `austral_liquid`, which depends on `austral_core`.
; `LiquidCheck` reaches `Compiler_plugin.verdict`, so it cannot live *inside*
; `austral_core` without a cycle.
;
; L10 Cycle B: `LiquidMeasure` is *extracted OCaml*, not hand-written. It comes
; from lib/liquid/subset/liquid_measure.mlw via
;
;   why3 extract -D lib/why3_plugin/unfer_ocaml.drv \
;     lib/liquid/subset/liquid_measure.mlw -o lib/liquid/LiquidMeasure.ml
;
; and is checked in so dune can compile it. A `verify-invariants` gate
; re-extracts and diffs, so it cannot drift from the Why3 source it came from;
; that gate is what makes checking in generated code defensible.
;
; Note the reuse: the extraction driver is lib/why3_plugin/unfer_ocaml.drv, the
; one unfer's S36 cycle already uses. It maps exactly this fragment (`int` to a
; native OCaml int, plus `bool` and `list`), so there is deliberately no
; liquid-specific driver.
(library
 (name austral_liquid)
 (public_name austral.austral_liquid)
 (synopsis "Liquid Austral: refinement types for the Total Austral Subset.")
 (libraries austral_core zarith str)
 (wrapped false)
 (flags :standard -w -39-50)
 (modules LiquidTypes LiquidParse LiquidConstraints LiquidInfer LiquidWhy3
          TotalityCheck LiquidCheck LiquidMeasure LiquidSubset))
